<title>INDIA: India Bajaj 96/97 1st half net up 27 pct.</title>
<headline>India Bajaj 96/97 1st half net up 27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   2,258.9    vs   1,775.8</p>
<p>    Net sales	   16,029.2    vs  12,810.5</p>
<p>    Share (in rupees)     56.47   vs	43.94</p>
<p>    Other income	 1,095.6    vs     757.7</p>
<p>    Total sales	 17,124.8    vs  13,568.2</p>
<p>    Total expenditure 13,079.3    vs  10,448.7</p>
<p>    Interest		  38.6    vs	41.8</p>
<p>    Gross profit	 4,006.9    vs   3,077.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   558.0    vs     406.9</p>
<p>    Tax		    1,190.0    vs     895.0</p>
<p>Note: Bajaj Auto said its exports in the first six months ending September 1996 totalled 875.1 million rupees against 932.1 million in the previous year. The firm's total two-wheeler and three-wheeler production and sales in the first half of 1996/97 was 758,599 vehicles and 722,467 vehicles respectively.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
